program leak_dict_literal_string

? Dict-literal discipline: owned f-string values transfer into the dict
? without a second copy (emitStringCopy frees the ephemeral temp after
? duplicating). Previously the temporary leaked once per iteration.

@ main ||:
	expected: []

	total: 0
	loop i:0 to 500 do
		d: dict = <"k": f"v-{i}">
		total = total + d.size()
	$
	print(total)
	expected.push("500")

	print(expected)
$
